---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Booking software for community pottery studios"
	description="Kilnbook helps community and membership pottery studios share kilns, let members book wheel time and run open-studio hours without the whiteboard."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For community studios</p>
				<h1>One studio, a hundred members, three kilns.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Community studios run on shared everything: shared wheels, shared shelves, shared kilns.
					Kilnbook keeps track of who booked what, whose work is in which load and who is in the
					building during open-studio hours.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A floor plan of a community studio with six wheels, work tables and a kiln room"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What gets hard as a membership studio grows</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Everyone wants the same wheel</h3>
					<p>
						Evenings and weekends fill up first. Members who arrive at 6pm find every wheel taken,
						and a sign-up sheet on the door does not stop anyone from staying an extra hour.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Nobody knows what is on the shelf</h3>
					<p>
						Pieces pile up on the bisque shelf with no name on them. Firing fees get counted by hand
						at the end of the month, and work sits in the pickup area for weeks.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes and members compete for space</h3>
					<p>
						A Tuesday wheel course needs eight wheels. Members need to know which hours are open
						studio and which are taken, without you sending a weekly email.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time members can book themselves</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment in one-hour blocks from
			their phone. You set how many hours each membership tier gets, how far ahead they can book and
			whether peak hours count double. A tablet by the door handles open-studio check-in, so you know
			who is in the building while the kilns are running.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel booking works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Shared kilns without the shared spreadsheet</h2>
		<p>
			Members log each piece when they set it on the bisque shelf and pay the firing fee by cubic
			inch or per piece. Every kiln gets its own queue for bisque and glaze loads, and when a load is
			unloaded, everyone with work in it gets a pickup text.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes that share the calendar</h2>
		<p>
			Run multi-week courses, Saturday drop-ins and class packs alongside memberships, all in the same
			place members book their wheel time. Students book, pay and reschedule without emailing you,
			waitlists fill cancelled seats on their own, and instructors see their roster from the studio
			tablet.
			<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a community studio?</h2>
		<p>
			Most community studios start on the Studio plan at $79 a month. It covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, class packs, waitlists and memberships, and
			pickup texts. Running a fourth kiln or a second location? Collective has no kiln limit.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Give your members the good wheel back.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
